\label{def:homotopy}

Let $x, y \in V(G)$.
Two dartwalks $w = (d_i)_{1 \leq i \leq m}$ and $w' = (d_i')_{1 \leq i \leq m'}$ from $x$ to $y$
are said to be \emph{homotopic} if
there exists a finite sequence $(w_j)_{1 \leq j \leq n}$ such that:
\begin{itemize}
  \item for all $1 \leq j \leq n$, $w_j$ is a
  dartwalk from $x$ to $y$;
  \item $w_1=w$ and $w_n=w'$;
  \item for any $1 \leq j < n$, either $w_j$ is a reduction of $w_{j+1}$ or $w_{j+1}$ is a
  reduction of $w_j$.
\end{itemize}

\label{def:universal_cover}

We define the \emph{universal cover} $\hat{G}$ of $(G,r)$, which is a rooted graph,
by letting:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $V(\hat G)$ be the set of non-backtracking dartwalks on $G$
  starting at $r$;
  \item the dartset $D(\hat{G})$ is defined as the set of pairs $(w,d)$ where
  $w$ is a non-backtracking dartwalk ($w \in V(\hat{G})$) and $d \in D(G)$
  is a dart on $G$ starting at the endpoint of $w$;
  \item for $(w,d) \in D(\hat{G})$, $\spt_{\hat{G}}(w,d) = w$,
  $\ept_{\hat{G}}(d) = (w \cdot d)_{\mathrm{nb}}$ and $\symm_{\hat{G}}(w,d) =
   ((w \cdot d)_{\mathrm{nb}},\symm_G(d))$;
  \item the root $\hat{r}$ is the empty walk from $r$ to $r$.
\end{itemize}

\label{thm:univ_cover_cover}

The projection map $\pi : \hat{G} \rightarrow G$ which is defined by $\pi(w)=\ept(w)$
for $w \in V(\hat G)$ and $\pi(w,d)=d$ for $(w,d) \in D(\hat G)$ is a covering map.

